{"kind":"request","text":"Harden the GitHub connector's HTTP transport (finding #5 of the 2026-08-11 security assessment at main 8f22ba52; re-verify at the implementation head). In internal/connector/github/fetch.go: (a) get() reads the body with an unbounded io.ReadAll (fetch.go:171) while Go transparently gzip-decompresses, so a small compressed response inflates without bound (decompression bomb); (b) List() (fetch.go:85-99) pages until an empty batch with no page or cumulative cap, so a misbehaving host loops until OOM (the pull-request filter means a non-empty page can contribute nothing, so 'no progress' is undetected); (c) the client (fetch.go:33) sets no CheckRedirect, so an https-\u003ehttp same-host redirect re-sends Authorization: Bearer \u003cPAT\u003e in cleartext. The sibling clients (cmd/gs boundedClient, cmd/gitseq-mcp newResidentClient) already do this correctly. Direction: bounded LimitReader with an explicit over-limit error, a page/total cap that logs what it dropped, and a no-redirect policy; do not attach the Bearer across a scheme downgrade or unrelated host.","body":{"conditions":"connector reads are size-bounded with an explicit over-limit error; pagination has a hard cap that is logged when hit; the HTTP client refuses redirects; the Bearer token is never re-sent across a scheme downgrade or unrelated host; make test and make race pass; request/ branch, independent review at an exact head before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 8f22ba52; re-verify citations at the implementation head"}}